# CI gate — do not finish until green

Before you report work as **done**, **complete**, or **ready to push**, run the same checks as `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:

```bash
# Windows
.\scripts\ci.ps1

# Linux / Pi / macOS
./scripts/ci.sh
```

Equivalent manual steps:

```bash
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install --upgrade -e ".[dev]"
pre-commit run --all-files
pyright
pytest -q -m "not live" --cov=rain_bypass --cov-fail-under=100
```

## Required workflow

1. After substantive edits (source, tests, scripts, workflow, pre-commit config), run the CI script.
2. If anything fails, fix it and re-run until all steps pass.
3. Only then commit, push, or tell the user the task is finished.

Do not skip this because tests alone passed — **pre-commit** (ruff, shellcheck, LF) and **pyright** must pass too. That is what failed in CI previously.

## When it applies

- New features, bug fixes, refactors, test changes, dependency or workflow edits.
- Skip only for pure docs with zero code/tooling changes, or when the user explicitly asks not to run checks.
